Q:
Find the following limit using either forms or continuity: lim as x -> infinity of ((x^7+1)^(1/3)-x)/(ln(x)+x^2)

A:
infinity

lim as x -> infinity of ((x^7+1)^(1/3)-x)/(ln(x)+x^2) ~ lim as x -> infinity of ((x^7)^(1/3)-x)/x^2

This simplifies further:

lim as x -> infinity of ((x^7)^(1/3)-x)/x^2 = lim as x -> infinity of x^(7/3)/x^2 = lim as x -> infinity of x^(7/3 - 2) = lim as x -> infinity of x^(7/3 - 6/3) = lim as x -> infinity of x^(1/3) = infinity

Thus lim as x -> infinity of ((x^7+1)^(1/3)-x)/(ln(x)+x^2) = infinity.

